# LS_COLORS — Kanagawa Dragon. Sourced by ~/.zshrc; do not hand-edit.
#
# vivid ships no Kanagawa theme, so unlike the previous two palettes this could
# not simply be `vivid generate <name>`. It is instead vivid's own
# `gruvbox-dark` output with the palette remapped to Dragon: vivid's filetype
# database is theme-independent (all its themes share the same ~677 rules and
# differ only in which colour each rule points at), so substituting the 17
# gruvbox colours for their Dragon counterparts, paired by the role each plays,
# yields a genuine Dragon LS_COLORS with full extension coverage.
#
# gruvbox-dark was chosen as the base because it is also a warm theme, so the
# role assignments already suit a warm palette. The mapping is recorded in the
# script that generated this — see the commit message.
#
# Directories are `yellow` #c4b28a, this setup's accent, which is the closest
# Dragon has to the warm sandy that the old Vesper config used for them.
#
# Regenerate by re-running that substitution over a fresh `vivid generate
# gruvbox-dark`; keep it a single export line so the diff stays one line.
#
# Note this is the *GNU* variable. BSD /bin/ls ignores it and reads LSCOLORS
# instead — see the note in .zshrc where that is set.

